{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_comment": "Plotter registry for hpgl-viewer. Field names match the shared registry in the cursor project so entries can be copied between them. All plotter coordinates are in native plotter units; 'units_per_mm' converts to millimetres. 'max_area' is the machine's maximum plot area (the furthest the pen can reach); 'margin' is a deliberate per-edge inset applied on top of it (positive shrinks that edge inward, negative extends past the maximum). The effective plot area is max_area inset by margin. HPGL files are authored in this same unit space, so these rectangles overlay a loaded drawing directly.",
  "_paper_comment": "'paper' describes the physical sheet, which hpgl-viewer draws around the plot area so you can see how much unreachable paper margin a drawing leaves. 'size_mm' is the sheet. 'offset_mm.left' is the distance in mm from the sheet's LEFT edge to max_area.x, and 'offset_mm.bottom' the distance from the sheet's BOTTOM edge to max_area.y — i.e. how far in from the paper edge the pen can first reach. Negative means the plot area runs off the sheet. Every offset below is a placeholder derived by centring the plot area on the sheet, which is only correct for machines whose max_area is symmetric about the origin; each entry is marked \"verified\": false until measured against a real plot. Measure a plot, put the real numbers here, and set \"verified\": true.",

